      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hello @{5de9405aea7cc52772fcc359|full_name} that sounds like a good strategy. I also wanted to know if it could be possible to read any custom created parameters that an author packs with the avatar? Essentially an avatar 3.0's toggles could influence a map if the author wishes to read the parameters, and if he/she knows the custom parameters.\nFor example, I create avatar A and have a parameter for showing a jetpack gameobject on the avatar itself. My world script would then read the parameters of the player's avatar and react appropriately by altering physics for that player.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-10T21:07:53.031Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There should be a method to read an avatar 3.0's parameters from the built-in parameters from ControlType,IsVR, etc to custom creator specified parameters.\n\nWhy?\nI am working on a map that will come with avatars that people should choose to be in order to play. I will be reading a parameter that is like the \"gate\" code to allow them to play. this reduces invisible/massive avatars from spoiling the competitive arena I am designing.\nNot only that, I will be adding a toggle or two that would not only change the look of the avatar, but also make the code behave differently for the avatar. I.e. Jetpack on/off.",
